WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.130
Harry Kersh: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:04.670
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:07.240
between Five Guys in the UK and the US.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.740
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:14.680
Burgers from a UK Five
Guys come in two sizes.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.200
Joe Avella: Five Guys in the
US also has two burger sizes.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.633
Harry: Firstly we have the little,

00:00:18.633 --> 00:00:20.174
which is just one patty.

00:00:20.174 --> 00:00:24.520
Joe: And the regular,
which is two patties.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.090
Harry: Now, our patties
are supposed to be lighter

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:29.210
than the US patties and
should weigh 67 grams.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:31.523
We're gonna weigh one and
find out if that's accurate.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:36.680
So, this patty actually weighed 52 grams,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:39.460
which is 15 grams less than
what we're supposed to get.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:41.700
Joe: According to the
US Five Guys website,

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.210
they say that one of the patties

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:46.900
should weigh 94 grams,
or about 3.3 ounces.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.680
We will weigh a hamburger patty

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.096
in the US Five Guys.

00:00:51.096 --> 00:00:54.421
That's about 52, 53 grams.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:56.300
It looks like our patties weigh

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.060
just about the same as the ones in the UK.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:00.151
Harry: We're not sure if they measure it

00:01:00.151 --> 00:01:02.140
before or after cooking.
Maybe it's before,

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:03.920
and then some of the
liquid leaves as it cooks,

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.780
but either way, not quite
what we're expecting.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:09.200
Joe: This right here is a
hot dog from a US Five Guys.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:13.008
And before I measure it,

00:01:13.008 --> 00:01:16.600
what in the heck is this?

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:17.633
Did you know this?

00:01:17.633 --> 00:01:19.700
They cut the hot dog in half?

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:21.890
I hate that they cut this in half.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.550
Cursed image.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.400
OK, how long is this monstrosity?

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.183
6 1/4 inches for the hot dog.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:32.540
Harry: So, a hot dog from a UK Five Guys

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:34.610
is about 6 inches in length.

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.730
Now, like the burgers, this
has an estimated weight,

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:38.930
and it should weigh 146 grams

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:41.640
if the website's ingredients
information is correct.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:43.790
But ours actually weighs 154 grams,

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:45.803
so we're actually getting
more than expected.

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:48.910
Joe: OK, let's weigh this thing

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:51.550
before I throw it in the ocean.

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:55.700
We're about a hair over 150. OK.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:57.810
I wanna talk to one of the Five Guys.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.910
Get me guy No. 3 or 4, I don't care.

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:03.920
I demand to know what is
going on with these hot dogs.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.670
A Five Guys chocolate milkshake in the US,

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:07.970
I believe it's 12 ounces,

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:11.440
let's see what it actually is here.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:12.556
This one's a little bit more,

00:02:12.556 --> 00:02:13.840
ooh, a little bit more melted.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:15.980
Whoa, whoa, whoa, wait,
wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:18.660
Oh, yeah. That's way more than 12, buddy.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.680
That's way more than 12.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:24.513
It is just over 450 milliliters.

00:02:24.513 --> 00:02:27.279
Almost 16 ounces.

00:02:27.279 --> 00:02:29.420
Harry: This is a milkshake
from a UK Five Guys.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:31.479
We're gonna measure it to
find out how much you get.

00:02:31.479 --> 00:02:32.808
Mm, bloop bloop bloop bloop.

00:02:32.808 --> 00:02:34.232
Oh, look how thick that is.

00:02:34.232 --> 00:02:35.448
Yes!

00:02:35.448 --> 00:02:37.220
I want it.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:38.362
Now, the UK portion size

00:02:38.362 --> 00:02:41.203
is advertised as 454 milliliters.

00:02:41.203 --> 00:02:43.320
We've got just over 400 here.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:44.540
If we scraped around the side,

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:46.450
we could probably get a
few more in there as well.

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:48.080
Now, Five Guys in the UK is notorious

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:49.880
for overfilling its fry portions.

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:51.088
We also get three sizes,

00:02:51.088 --> 00:02:52.921
little, regular, and large.

00:02:52.921 --> 00:02:55.010
We ordered all three,
and they came in one bag,

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:56.160
and here's what we got.

00:02:57.542 --> 00:02:58.742
Little fries,

00:03:00.583 --> 00:03:01.766
regular fries,

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:04.324
large fries,

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.336
and this is the rest of the bag.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.100
Now, we're not sure which of these fries

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.340
belongs to which of these portions,

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:13.890
so we're gonna try and figure it out.

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:15.920
Joe: In the US, we also
have three sizes of fries

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.520
at the Five Guys.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:18.845
The small,

00:03:20.779 --> 00:03:21.987
the regular,

00:03:23.912 --> 00:03:25.528
the large,

00:03:25.528 --> 00:03:26.636
and, yes,

00:03:26.636 --> 00:03:29.970
so many more fries. Look at that.

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:31.328
So, all in all,

00:03:31.328 --> 00:03:33.519
Five Guys is very generous with the fries.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:38.440
Harry: I mean, I guess I'll
start by filling each cup,

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:39.760
and then try and portion this

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:43.700
into, like, vague threes, I guess.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:47.100
Joe: Yes, that sounds right,
I don't know if it is,

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.460
but I'm just gonna follow
Harry's lead on this one.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:50.870
Harry: So, this is roughly what we think

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.680
would go with each of the portions.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:54.380
Now, in the UK, a regular fries

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.950
is supposed to weigh 414 grams.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:59.130
We're gonna weigh the cup
and then also the extras

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.280
to see if what you get really is a bonus

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:04.630
or if it actually all adds
up to the supposed total.

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:07.720
165.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.700
Joe: So, first we'll do the scale, right?

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:12.340
So, this is supposed to be 411 grams.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:13.830
Let's see what we got.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:15.800
What is this, 170?

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:18.010
Woof, guys. That's not even close.

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:19.420
Harry: So, our regular cup of fries

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:21.680
actually only contained 165 grams,

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:24.000
which is less than half of
what you're supposed to get.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.490
We're gonna weigh the rest of the fries

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:27.382
to see if that makes up the difference.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.610
So, even with all the bag fries,

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:31.770
which we assigned to the regular portion,

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:34.080
we're still only looking at 276 grams,

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.530
which is well below the portion size

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:37.280
you're supposed to be
getting for a regular.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:40.020
Joe: Excellent idea,
Harry, I will do the same.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:41.795
Now we are up to...

00:04:41.795 --> 00:04:43.870
275?

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:46.270
Still not even -- it's supposed 411?

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:47.394
Harry: So, it looks like we've been a bit

00:04:47.394 --> 00:04:48.750
shortchanged on the fries.

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:50.610
Because it was all given
to us in one big bag,

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:52.780
it's hard to tell which
portion came out small.

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:53.880
So what we're gonna do is

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:55.750
add the little fries to this one,

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:57.780
get a total figure for all three portions,

00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:58.755
and then figure out how much

00:04:58.755 --> 00:05:00.950
we've been shortchanged overall.

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:01.783
So, we've done the maths,

00:05:01.783 --> 00:05:04.670
and between our large,
regular, and little fries,

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:07.970
including the bag fries,
we only got 830 grams.

00:05:07.970 --> 00:05:11.800
However, we were supposed
to get 1,220 grams,

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:13.080
which means we've been shortchanged

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.340
by roughly a third here.

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:17.260
Frygate 2020!

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:21.160
Joe: Technically, Harry,
this is Frygate 2021.

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:22.730
Check the release schedule.

00:05:22.730 --> 00:05:26.210
With the rest of the bag fries,
the large, and the little,

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:31.101
so, they gave us 851 grams of fries

00:05:31.101 --> 00:05:32.250
total.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:35.440
They're supposed to give us 1,225.

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:36.848
Hey, Siri,

00:05:36.848 --> 00:05:40.073
851 is what percentage

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:42.848
of 1,225?

00:05:42.848 --> 00:05:46.130
Siri: About 69.4693%.

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.780
Joe: 69%.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.750
Nice.

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:50.810
Harry: So, at least in our case,

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:53.497
it seems as if the generosity of Five Guys

00:05:53.497 --> 00:05:54.920
has been a bit overstated.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.970
Maybe they just overfill
smaller containers

00:05:56.970 --> 00:05:59.180
so you kind of think you're
getting more than you should be,

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:00.790
whereas in reality, if you measure it all,

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:02.540
you're actually maybe getting less.

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:07.650
Joe: Let's compare the
prices of both Five Guys

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:09.270
and see who's getting the better deal.

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:13.530
OK, USA, this hamburger costs $9.12.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:16.290
That is way too much
money for this burger.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:17.850
Harry: A hamburger from a UK Five Guys

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:19.720
will cost you 6 pounds 95,

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:23.070
which is equivalent to $9.20.

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:24.580
Joe: The prices do seem similar,

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:27.970
but it's actually per
gram 26% less in the US

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:29.020
than it is in the UK.

00:06:30.059 --> 00:06:31.080
Harry: What about the fries?

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:34.220
Well, in the UK, a large
fries is 5 pounds 25,

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:37.250
which comes to $6.95.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:40.100
Joe: In the US, our Five
Guys large after tax

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:42.075
is $7.06.

00:06:42.075 --> 00:06:44.720
You must be joking.

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:46.320
Harry: If you do the maths for the fries,

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.250
it turns out that the US
is getting a better deal,

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:49.340
but only fractionally.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:51.530
You guys get, like, 1%
more value for your money

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:52.640
when it comes to the large fries,

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.310
so, not too mad about that one.

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:57.440
Producer: A big draw is that
when you're in Five Guys,

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:00.640
they have just crates open with peanuts,

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:01.750
and while you're waiting your food,

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.180
you can just scoop some peanuts

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:04.705
and just, like, crack the shells open --

00:07:04.705 --> 00:07:05.610
Joe: What do you even mean?

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:06.980
So if you go into the store and you wait,

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:09.560
you can eat, like, you
can peel and eat peanuts

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:11.340
and, what, throw the shells on the floor,

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:13.420
like it's a saloon in the 1800s?

00:07:13.420 --> 00:07:15.430
Who cares? Especially if
you're going there to eat,

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:17.060
let me fill up in these cheap peanuts

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:19.210
before I get this
ridiculously priced food.

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:22.030
Harry: Compared to some of
the places that we reviewed

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:23.120
on this show before,

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:24.840
Five Guys is a more expensive option,

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:26.570
but, I mean, particularly in the UK,

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:28.430
I don't feel too mad
about paying a bit more

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:31.030
for a Five Guys than I might
do for a meal at McDonald's.

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:31.940
It's just more of a treat,

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:33.750
but it does feel a bit more exotic,

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:34.770
they've branded themselves

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:36.310
as a kind of, like, American import,

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:38.710
Americans-know-their-way-
around-a-burger sort of thing.

00:07:38.710 --> 00:07:40.740
So if I go, I know that
I'm getting something

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:41.770
of a little bit higher quality

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:43.550
than maybe a standard fast-food place,

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:46.750
even if the prices are gonna cost me more.

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:47.870
Joe: I hate Five Guys.

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:49.290
The hot dog is ridiculous,

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:50.560
I don't care about peanuts,

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:52.783
this stuff is way overpriced, forget it.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:56.243
Let's take a look at the calories

00:07:56.243 --> 00:07:57.950
of the Five Guys cheeseburger.

00:07:57.950 --> 00:07:59.060
This has two patties,

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:00.865
two slices of cheese, and a bun,

00:08:00.865 --> 00:08:03.783
and the total calories is 984.

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:06.330
Harry: What about a UK cheeseburger?

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:09.120
Well, this one comes to 756 calories,

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:12.220
which is more than 200 calories
less than the US burger.

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:14.200
The US burger doesn't just
have more calories, either;

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:15.770
it's got pretty much
more of everything else.

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:18.080
It's got more fat, saturates, and sodium

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:19.950
than a cheeseburger in the UK.

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:21.350
In the UK, if they actually give you

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:22.830
what's advertised on the website,

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:27.240
a large portion of fries
is a hefty 1,491 calories.

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:28.090
But despite that,

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:30.231
we still somehow end up with less sodium.

00:08:30.231 --> 00:08:33.610
Joe: Our large fry in
the US is 1,314 calories.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:34.451
I also want to point out

00:08:34.451 --> 00:08:36.310
our fries come in lower than the UK

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:39.230
in terms of fat content
as well as saturates.

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:40.530
And, finally, we have the drinks.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:42.567
This chocolate shake at
a Five Guys in the US

00:08:42.567 --> 00:08:44.283
is 830 calories.

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:47.320
Harry: A chocolate shake in
the UK comes to slightly more,

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:49.820
at 891 calories.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:51.800
Joe: So, what if we combine
all three into a meal?

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:53.620
So, a plain cheeseburger, regular fries,

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:55.820
and a chocolate shake
from Five Guys in the US

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:59.895
totals at 2,767 calories.

00:08:59.895 --> 00:09:01.370
Yo, dog!

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:04.500
Also, I think this is about $70. [laughs]

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:05.850
Harry: The same meal in the UK?

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:09.940
Well, that comes to a
total of 2,769 calories,

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:12.330
two calories more than in the US.

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:14.520
The differences between
the burger and the fries

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:16.220
effectively cancel each other out.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.170
Let's start with the basics.

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:22.900
Here's everything in a hamburger patty

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:24.630
from a UK Five Guys.

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:25.780
Ground beef.

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:29.981
Joe: Here in the US, our
burger patty is made up of

00:09:29.981 --> 00:09:31.301
ground beef.

00:09:31.301 --> 00:09:33.410
[crickets chirping]

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:35.010
Harry: If you prefer to
add cheese to your burger,

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:37.400
here's what's in the cheese in the UK.

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:40.970
Cheddar cheese, water, butter, cheese,

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:42.882
milk proteins, whey powder,

00:09:42.882 --> 00:09:45.749
emulsifying salt (trisodium citrate),

00:09:45.749 --> 00:09:48.650
natural cheese flavoring,
salt, lactic acid,

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:51.800
sorbic acid, beta-carotene,
paprika extract,

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:53.810
and sunflower lecithin.

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:56.320
Joe: Five Guys cheese here
in the US is made up of:

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:59.610
milk, whey, milk fat,
milk protein concentrate,

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:02.470
salt, calcium phosphate, sodium citrate,

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:04.123
whey protein concentrate,

00:10:04.123 --> 00:10:06.368
sodium phosphate, sorbic acid,

00:10:06.368 --> 00:10:07.264
[error ping]

00:10:07.264 --> 00:10:09.247
apple-call-a-tent-all? What?

00:10:10.138 --> 00:10:13.088
Apo...car-oh-ten-all?

00:10:13.088 --> 00:10:14.686
Apocatarnenal.

00:10:14.686 --> 00:10:16.461
Annatto, enzymes,

00:10:16.461 --> 00:10:19.561
vitamin D3, and cheese cultures.

00:10:19.561 --> 00:10:21.410
Harry: The burger buns
are also pretty similar.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:24.110
In the UK, a burger bun is made with:

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:27.360
wheat flour, water, sugar, vegetable fat,

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:31.130
milk, dry yeast, eggs, sesame seeds, salt,

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:34.330
soya flour, calcium
carbonate, and spirit vinegar.

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:35.800
Joe: The bun in the US is made up of:

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:38.370
water, salt, sugar, vegetable shortening,

00:10:38.370 --> 00:10:40.878
milk, eggs, bleached bread flour,

00:10:40.878 --> 00:10:43.044
yeast, and sesame seeds.

00:10:43.044 --> 00:10:44.120
Harry: Now, you'd think that the fries

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:45.550
would be pretty similar
in the two countries,

00:10:45.550 --> 00:10:47.030
and for the most part you'd be right.

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:49.100
In the UK, the fries are made of potatoes,

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:50.535
peanut oil, and salt.

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:53.470
Joe: The fries at the Five Guys in the US

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:56.610
are made from potatoes,
refined peanut oil, and salt.

00:10:56.610 --> 00:10:58.500
Now, when they say "refined peanut oil,"

00:10:58.500 --> 00:11:01.180
apparently the peanut oil
in the UK is not refined.

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:02.380
Here in the US it is.

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:04.290
What that means is they do
something with distillation

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:05.960
or neutralization, I don't even know,

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:07.000
but the reason they do it

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.290
is to give it a better shelf life

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:09.620
and a more uniform taste.

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:13.120
This has been the greasiest
"Food Wars" I've ever done.

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:15.490
So they are very generous
with the peanut oil

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:17.900
on the fries and pretty
much everything else.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:19.240
Harry: There are a few
things to watch out for

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:20.370
on the menu at Five Guys.

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:22.490
For example, the pickles in the US.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:24.450
In the US, the pickles
contain a food coloring

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:26.800
called Yellow 5, or tartrazine.

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:29.200
If this is added to foods
in the European Union,

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:30.190
they have to have a warning

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:33.660
saying that they might cause
hyperactivity in children.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:35.350
Joe: Yes, our pickles have
a bunch of junk in it,

00:11:35.350 --> 00:11:38.080
so does the relish.
Specifically, it is made up of:

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:41.690
cucumbers, corn syrup, water,
high-fructose corn syrup,

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:46.220
vinegar, salt, xanthan gum,
0.1% of sodium benzoate

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:48.920
as a preservative, calcium chloride, alum,

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:52.153
natural flavors, polysorbate 80,

00:11:52.153 --> 00:11:54.828
Yellow No. 5, and maltol.

00:11:57.500 --> 00:11:59.470
Harry: In our shortest
exclusives section yet,

00:11:59.470 --> 00:12:01.080
here is everything you
can only find on the menu

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:03.000
at a UK Five Guys.

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:04.430
Joe: And here are all the exclusive

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:07.010
Five Guys menu items in the US.

00:12:07.010 --> 00:12:08.250
Harry: Let's start with the burger.

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:09.750
There's only one option in the UK

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.570
that you won't be able to find in the US,

00:12:11.570 --> 00:12:13.640
and that is HP Sauce.

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:14.700
I won't go into too much detail

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:17.060
in case Joe accuses me
of Brit-splaining again,

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:19.090
but for those who don't
know, HP sauce is like a --

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:20.920
Joe: The only customization in the US

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:22.310
that you can't get in the UK

00:12:22.310 --> 00:12:23.560
is actually something

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:24.860
that everyone in the United States

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:26.380
knows exactly what I'm talking about,

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:29.740
and that is A1 steak sauce.

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:32.100
It looks a lot like the HP
brown sauce, but it is not.

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:34.170
It doesn't taste anything like it.

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:38.277
It is the most popular steak sauce.

00:12:40.512 --> 00:12:44.930
Ad: A1. It's how steak is done.

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:47.450
Joe: I don't know if it even
exists outside of the US.

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:49.630
Harry: The rest of our exclusive
options come as drinks,

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:50.820
such as milkshakes.

00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:52.500
We have a biscuit shake,

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:54.290
which is flavored with Biscoff biscuits,

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:56.020
which are those little
caramel-flavored cookies

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:58.110
which you get on the
side of a tea or coffee.

00:12:58.110 --> 00:12:59.910
Then we have three dessert shake options,

00:12:59.910 --> 00:13:01.940
which are milkshakes flavored with things

00:13:01.940 --> 00:13:05.050
which kind of combine to
replicate famous desserts.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:09.493
So, here we have a millionaire's
shortbread milkshake.

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:13.500
Here we have a banoffee pie milkshake.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:16.790
And here we have a strawberry
cheesecake milkshake.

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:17.700
Joe: Now, for the last thing,

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:19.098
the only shake you can get in the US

00:13:19.098 --> 00:13:20.960
that you can't get in the UK is this,

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:23.160
it is the Oreo, listen
to me when I say it,

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:24.850
let me finish before you start typing,

00:13:24.850 --> 00:13:27.970
an Oreo Double Stuf milkshake.

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:30.020
Yes, you guys have the Oreo shake there,

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:32.830
and I think you also have an
Oreo cream shake there too,

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:35.880
but this is the only
Oreo Double Stuf shake.

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:38.030
If you don't have Oreo
Double Stuf in the UK,

00:13:38.030 --> 00:13:39.180
they're what they sound like,

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:41.790
Oreos with twice as much filling.

00:13:41.790 --> 00:13:43.670
This is the last thing
we're shooting today,

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:45.833
and I've been waiting for this all day.

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:50.536
Holy s---, this is so good.

00:13:50.536 --> 00:13:52.370
[producer laughing]
Guys, I'm not playing,

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:53.680
this might've turned the tides

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:55.290
on how I feel about Five Guys.

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:57.430
I'm not kidding, this is so good.

00:13:57.430 --> 00:13:58.263
I'm finishing this.

00:13:58.263 --> 00:14:00.670
I don't care how sick it
makes me, I'm drinking it.

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:02.180
Harry: And last but by no means least,

00:14:02.180 --> 00:14:04.697
in the UK, you can wash
your burgers down with...

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.213
a range of beers.

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:12.205
Cheers.

00:14:18.220 --> 00:14:20.690
Joe: Yeah, well, they don't
serve beer at our Five Guys,

00:14:20.690 --> 00:14:22.213
but I brought my own.

00:14:24.310 --> 00:14:25.705
Cheers, my man.

00:14:28.624 --> 00:14:29.740
Ah.

00:14:29.740 --> 00:14:30.981
It is very warm.

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:33.872
It's a half a hot dog. That's split?

00:14:33.872 --> 00:14:35.113
It's like, I'm still like, what?

00:14:35.113 --> 00:14:37.640
I'm, like, I'm shook by that.

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:39.630
This is why people on the
internet now are like,

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:41.340
"I think a hot dog's a sandwich."

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:43.150
Well, when you serve it like that,

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:45.570
like with the meat cut in half like that,

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:47.370
it's like, yeah, it kinda
looks, but it's not!

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:48.420
It's a hot dog.

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:50.490
And you don't cut it down
the middle like that.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:51.553
It's ridiculous.

